        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "6 inches to cm.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "15 cm",
          "worked": "Read up from 6 inches to the line, then across to the centimetres axis: 15 cm.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "20 cm to inches.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "8 inches",
          "worked": "Read across from 20 cm to the line, then down to the inches axis: 8 inches.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the gradient, use the point $(10,25)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2.5$",
          "worked": "Using $(0,0)$ and $(10,25)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}m&=\\frac{25-0}{10-0}\\\\m&=2.5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "What does the gradient represent?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "2.5 cm per inch",
          "worked": "Each increase of 1 inch corresponds to an increase of 2.5 cm. The gradient is the conversion factor, 2.5 cm per inch.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Write an equation relating centimetres and inches. Using your equation, how many inches is 200 cm?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "80 inches",
          "worked": "Let $C$ be the number of centimetres and $I$ the number of inches.\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=2.5I\\\\200&=2.5I\\\\I&=\\frac{200}{2.5}\\\\I&=80\\end{align*}$$\n200 cm is 80 inches according to the graph's model.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      }
    ],
